      "content": "exactly. so if the model is essentially using the zip code as a proxy/tie-breaker, isn't it basically just pricing in the demographic makeup of those neighborhoods? like, if Cedar Grove has a higher concentration of certain ethnic groups or lower socioeconomic indicators, doesn't the model end up penalizing the individual for the community's profile rather than their own actual creditworthiness? how would you justify that in an audit?",
